hostdisk.device for booting AROS from an image file on Hosted MacAROS.

- hostdisk=PATTERN on the kernel command line replaces the host path of
  unit N (/dev/disk%ld); the pattern must hold one %ld and no other
  conversion. Without it the device probes the Mac's own drives.
- Darwin on Apple Silicon: struct stat in place of the 32-bit inode
  request, which the SDK refuses, and the two DKIOC requests of
  <sys/disk.h> spelled out, since that header cannot be included.

Local to this machine's AROS tree (jonx/AROS, aarch64-darwin-graft); it
is not pushed anywhere. Apply from the AROS source root with
git apply, then build workbench-devs-hostdisk.

diff --git a/arch/all-darwin/hostdisk/geometry.c b/arch/all-darwin/hostdisk/geometry.c
